From c7dac9298c1db781498cca68ac65f80a5ff41909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jdistler <josephcd921@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:30:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] demux: survive garbage 33-bit-max first PCR + PCR-starved
 force-playlist re-anchor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first HLS panelfuzz round found 6 fullent channels persistently freezing
video ~10s in over HLS (audio playing on, state Playing forever) while the same
channels play clean over raw TS. Two stacked defects, fixed together
(hls-investigation-log Iteration S; deterministic repro:
streamlab server.py snapshot + fullent/dailyshow-hls-snapshot):

1. ts.c PCRHandle: the transcoder family stamps ~0x1FFFFFFFF (~95443s) as the
   FIRST PCR of a session/segment while the PES timeline starts near 0 (fullent
   HLS seg0: PCR=8589871592, PES=0.13s — the same garbage value the side/trex
   guards 0025/0026 handle mid-stream). Latched as the reference it poisons the
   era: the next real PCR false-unwraps to 95443s+, and stock VLC only survives
   via the pcroffset kludge (+95443s on every block), which composes fatally
   with adaptive-ts-force-playlist. Drop a near-max FIRST sample once
   (marker "skywave-ts-pcr-spike: dropping near-max FIRST PCR"); a genuine
   about-to-wrap stream emits near-max again immediately and latches on the
   second sample (one harmless drop; verified: bloomberg-pcr-wrap unchanged).
   Raw-TS opens pre-latch pcr.i_first in the open-time probe, so this guard
   engages on the probe-less adaptive inner demux — where the bug lives —
   leaving validated raw-TS behavior untouched.

2. FakeESOut forceContinuity (adaptive-ts-force-playlist): the continuation
   high-water advanced ONLY on PCR, but on a PCR-starved mux (~1 PCR per 10s
   segment — and seg0's only PCR was the dropped garbage) it stagnated while
   seconds of ES flowed; the next segment's legitimate PCR then looked like a
   >1s forward discontinuity against the stale mark and spuriously re-anchored
   BACKWARD, mapping the new segment onto the already-played range — every
   frame discarded as past. New fp_last_any (all-outputs high-water) is used
   for the jump test and as the re-anchor target floor; fp_last_out stays
   PCR-driven for per-sample semantics (the earlier per-ES re-anchor runaway
   stays fixed).

Also fixed en route (same wedge, earlier layer): the es_out forced-rebuffer
reset (late PCR > jitter) killed the pipeline unrecoverably; with these two
fixes the adaptive pipeline never runs just-in-time on this shape, the late-PCR
path never triggers, and the repro plays 48s flawlessly (dec/disp lockstep,
zero lost, zero resets — was: wedge at 10.6s, 110 lost, dead recovery).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Happy <yesreply@happy.engineering>
---
 modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp | 32 ++++++++++++++++---
 modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.hpp |  3 ++
 modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c                       | 25 +++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp b/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp
index ac9c854fd0..54154779da 100644
--- a/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp
+++ b/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.cpp
@@ -617,11 +617,31 @@ vlc_tick_t FakeESOut::forceContinuity(vlc_tick_t ts, bool reanchor)
     if(reanchor)
     {
         vlc_tick_t cand = ts + fp_offset;
-        if(cand < fp_last_out || cand - fp_last_out > FP_DISCONTINUITY)
+        /* Two direction-specific marks (2026-07-13, the fullent HLS wedge):
+         * - BACKWARD test stays against fp_last_out (the PCR high-water): a normal
+         *   in-order PCR always trails the leading ES by its natural lead, so
+         *   testing backward against the all-outputs mark re-anchors on EVERY
+         *   sample — the runaway drift documented below.
+         * - FORWARD test runs against fp_last_any (the all-outputs high-water):
+         *   on a PCR-STARVED mux (fullent HLS: ~1 PCR per 10s segment — and the
+         *   first one can be the dropped 33-bit-max garbage, leaving a whole
+         *   segment with NO PCR at all) fp_last_out stagnates while seconds of ES
+         *   flow; the next segment's legitimate PCR then looked like a >1s forward
+         *   "discontinuity" against the stale PCR mark and spuriously re-anchored
+         *   BACKWARD, mapping the new segment onto the already-played range —
+         *   every frame discarded as past, video dead while audio played on. */
+        vlc_tick_t fwdmark = (fp_last_any != VLC_TICK_INVALID && fp_last_any > fp_last_out)
+                           ? fp_last_any : fp_last_out;
+        if(cand < fp_last_out || cand - fwdmark > FP_DISCONTINUITY)
         {
             /* Segment-boundary PTS reset: continue the output right after the last
-             * frame so the clock never jumps. (gap 0 => non-decreasing.) */
-            fp_offset = fp_last_out - ts;
+             * frame so the clock never jumps. (gap 0 => non-decreasing.) The target
+             * is the all-outputs mark: on a PCR-starved mux the PCR-only point can
+             * sit a whole segment behind the emitted timeline, and continuing from
+             * there would collide with already-played output. Worst case vs the
+             * PCR-only target is a one-time forward step of the leading ES's
+             * natural lead — bounded, unlike per-ES re-anchoring (see below). */
+            fp_offset = fwdmark - ts;
         }
     }
     vlc_tick_t out = ts + fp_offset;
@@ -631,9 +651,13 @@ vlc_tick_t FakeESOut::forceContinuity(vlc_tick_t ts, bool reanchor)
      * continue from whichever ES is furthest ahead, dragging the clock forward and the other
      * ES behind — a runaway A/V divergence (audio races seconds ahead → "playing silence"
      * waves; video falls seconds behind → "picture too late"). Tracking the PCR alone keeps
-     * each ES at its natural lead/lag relative to the clock, so A/V stay locked. */
+     * each ES at its natural lead/lag relative to the clock, so A/V stay locked.
+     * fp_last_any additionally tracks EVERY output (ES included) — used only by the
+     * jump test / re-anchor target above, never to drive per-sample re-anchoring. */
     if(reanchor && out > fp_last_out)
         fp_last_out = out;
+    if(fp_last_any == VLC_TICK_INVALID || out > fp_last_any)
+        fp_last_any = out;
     return out;
 }
 
diff --git a/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.hpp b/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.hpp
index b6dc2cdaff..ef57dd0c73 100644
--- a/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.hpp
+++ b/modules/demux/adaptive/plumbing/FakeESOut.hpp
@@ -164,6 +164,9 @@ namespace adaptive
             bool fp_have_ref = false;
             vlc_tick_t fp_offset = 0;
             vlc_tick_t fp_last_out = VLC_TICK_INVALID;
+            /* all-outputs high-water (ES included) — jump-test/re-anchor-target
+             * only, never drives per-sample re-anchoring (see forceContinuity) */
+            vlc_tick_t fp_last_any = VLC_TICK_INVALID;
             /* Skywave (patch 0022): audio-video PES PTS offset detector +
              * compensator (adaptive/HLS side). Peer to the es_out.c detector but
              * ESSENTIAL for HLS because audio blocks with far-future PTS sit in
diff --git a/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c b/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
index 15cadd774f..26058bd4a5 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
+++ b/modules/demux/mpeg/ts.c
@@ -2467,6 +2467,31 @@ static void PCRHandle( demux_t *p_demux, ts_pid_t *pid, ts_90khz_t i_pcr )
                 ? PIDReferencedByProgram( p_pmt, pid->i_pid )
                 : ( p_pmt->i_pid_pcr == pid->i_pid );
 
+        /* Skywave (2026-07-13, round 3): drop a garbage near-33-bit-max FIRST PCR.
+         * The same transcoder family stamps ~0x1FFFFFFFF (~95443s) as the very first
+         * PCR of a session/segment while the PES timeline starts near 0 (fullent HLS
+         * seg0: PCR=8589871592, PES≈0.1s; also the widespread pcr-near-max-start
+         * shape on raw TS). Latched as the reference it poisons everything: the next
+         * real PCR (~9s) false-unwraps to the 95443s era, PES/PCR diverge by 26h, and
+         * stock VLC only survives via the pcroffset kludge (+95443s to every block) —
+         * which composes fatally with :adaptive-ts-force-playlist on HLS (the es_out
+         * forced-rebuffer wedge, hls-investigation-log Iteration S). A LEGITIMATE
+         * stream lands this close to the wrap point with ~1/3000 odds and then keeps
+         * emitting near-max PCRs (it wraps within seconds) — so: drop a near-max
+         * FIRST sample once; if the NEXT sample is also near-max (a genuine
+         * about-to-wrap stream), it latches normally, costing one harmless sample. */
+        if( b_is_program_pcr
+         && p_pmt->pcr.i_current == VLC_TICK_INVALID
+         && p_pmt->pcr.i_first == VLC_TICK_INVALID
+         && p_pmt->pcr.skywave_pcr_reject_streak == 0
+         && i_pcr > (ts_90khz_t)0x1FFFFFFFF - 30 * 90000 )
+        {
+            msg_Warn( p_demux, "skywave-ts-pcr-spike: dropping near-max FIRST PCR "
+                      "%"PRId64" (33-bit ceiling garbage)", (int64_t)i_pcr );
+            p_pmt->pcr.skywave_pcr_reject_streak++;
+            continue;
+        }
+
         /* Skywave (2026-07-13): drop a garbage forward-outlier PCR spike before it
          * updates pcr.i_current. Some Xtream transcoders emit ONE spurious PCR at the
          * 33-bit maximum (~95443s) at an encoder restart, then reset the real PCR+PES
-- 
